Card 1 is 6, and 15 cards remain with a total value of 80. Each unseen card is therefore worth 80/15 ≈ 5.33 on average. The two hidden cards are worth about 10.67 together, so the expected settlement is about 16.7.

The sum of the two hidden cards has a standard deviation of about 7.4. That means informed traders could cost me a lot. The share of informed traders is also unknown, and averages about 0.48 across the three possible values. So I'll quote a fairly wide spread centred on 16.7.

