Fair value is about 16.1. The deck sums to 86 over 16 cards, so each card averages 5.375, and three cards average about 16.1. The standard deviation of the three-card sum is about 8.5, which is large.

The share of informed traders could still be high. The only trade so far was a sale to me at 9.1, and that round settled at 7, which looks like an informed seller. Because the sum varies so much, I'll keep the spread wide. The last quote (10.5 / 21.7) got no trade, so I'll tighten slightly around 16.

{"bid": 11.0, "ask": 21.2}

Expected sum is about 18.08: die 1 averages 9.25 and die 2 averages about 8.83. The standard deviation is about 2.16.

The share of informed traders (alpha) is unknown and averages about 0.48 across the three possibilities. So I quote a fairly wide spread, about 1.4 on each side of fair value. That limits losses to informed traders while still catching some noise flow.

