I'm quoting a bid of 16.7 and an ask of 19.5 around a fair value of about 18.08.

- **Fair value:** die 1 averages 9.25 and die 2 averages 53/6 ≈ 8.83, so the sum is about 18.08.
- **Who I'm trading against:** I think the counterparties are mostly noise traders, so alpha is most likely 0.05. Four fills were at prices an informed trader would never accept, because they sold to me below the eventual settlement value:
  - round 1 sold at 16.8, settled at 19;
  - round 2 sold at 16.6, settled at 17;
  - round 4 sold at 16.7, settled at 19;
  - round 5 sold at 16.7 and 18.7, settled at 21.

  Only one fill (round 4, bought at 17.5, settled at 19) fits an informed trader.
- **Spread width:** Against noise with a standard deviation of 1.8, the profit per side, h·(1−Φ(h/1.8)), is highest at a half-spread of about 0.75σ ≈ 1.35. That puts the quotes around 16.7 and 19.5.

