Fair value is about 18.3. The expected card value is 67/11 ≈ 6.09, and three cards sum to about 18.27, with a standard deviation of roughly 5.3.

We don't know what fraction of counterparties are informed, and round 1 gave little evidence either way. So I'm quoting fairly wide around fair value. The spread is meant to guard against informed traders while still giving noise traders some chance to trade.

