Card 1 is a 3. The remaining 10 cards are one 1, three 3s, two 7s and four 10s, so each unseen card averages 6.4. That puts expected settlement at about 3 + 12.8 = 15.8.

Almost every past trade went against the settlement value, which an informed trader would never do. So alpha is very likely 0.05, and I'm almost entirely facing noise traders (standard deviation 3.7). Against them, a half-spread of about 2.7 roughly maximises expected profit per quote. Because I'm short 1, I shift both prices slightly up.

